    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to the Humanist Hour, the official podcast of the American Humanist Association. In this episode, talking humanist politics with a United States Senator, my confusion over our national motto, and the illegality of taking up Enferra Leo on a cinematic outing, all coming up on this episode of The Humanist Hour. Hello everybody, my name is Beau Bennett and I'm your host for this week's episode of The Humanist Hour. If you ever wondered why, science is so clear on some issues, yet there are still laws in effect that are completely against the science, or even worse than that, the law still might be in effect, but the people still support these laws. Even though the science might say something completely different. Well, if you lived in the country for, I don't know, any more than a few days, you'd probably understand that the country and our laws within this country do not work based off of science. This isn't a science-driven country. This isn't a fact-driven country. And if you watch the news, well, there's a hint right there that that might not be the case. I thought instead of having somebody talking about science or critical thinking like we usually do, let's get somebody on who knows a little something about politics. And yeah, we could have gotten anybody. You know, we could have, there's so many people that talk about politics, but we went pretty much straight. Actually, we went to the very top president of the United States and then we backed up a couple because frankly, we just couldn't get the president of the United States. But who did we get? We got Maryland State Senator Jamie Raskin, an attorney and professor of constitutional law who has earned national recognition as a civil rights and civil liberties advocate. He was actually honored by the American Humanist Association back in 2008 with its distinguished service award at the World Humanist Congress in Washington, D.C. he has an article on the humanist dot com if you just google his name and humanist you'll find it and it's a fascinating article here's a fascinating gentleman and that i said you know what we need to get on the humanist our podcast so i did and here's my interview with senator jamie raskin and i have the great pleasure of speaking with senator jamie raskin how are you sir Excellent. Hey, the pleasure is all mine. Thank you for having me on the show. All right. Can you start by telling our listeners a little bit about yourself?",
