    "turn_text": "Well, that's true. In essence, I mean, it was, it was hot to, you know, be exchange, I mean, you get It was a little tough on me because when I got elected to the Senate I sat next to Nancy Jacobs and you know I got a ton of reaction to it and she got a ton of reaction to it too but we ended up being friends and actually when she ended up leaving the Maryland Senate I was one of the senators I was the Democratic Senator who you know praised her and her her devotion to her constituents and you know in her beliefs but obviously we we had a lot to discuss over the years, and we had some serious clashes. But yeah, what I said was basic Jeffersonianism. I mean, that here the Constitution governs not the Bible. And you can swear on the Bible, as we were saying before, but you're swearing to uphold the Constitution, not vice versa.",
