  {
    "episode_id": 84720,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84720.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "Initially when I thought of climate change as an issue, I thought that it was pretty simple. I thought there was one side and there was the science side of it and of course science clearly shows that there's a problem. There's really no debate there and then there's the political side of it Now that we know that there's a problem, what should we do about it? And I really thought that that was the problem. But as you clearly stated, that isn't the issue. It's not that everybody knows climate change is a problem and everybody agrees with the very clear science. There are many people out there who, very smart people, politicians who just completely deny the science. Do you find that a lot? And who are these deniers exactly?",
