    "turn_text": "yeah well you know that the supreme court in the hurricane said that people have a right to individual gun ownership for the purposes of hunting and recreation and that's acknowledged and of course for the purposes of participating in the militia which was the position of the liberal dissenters, of course, that the second on the right should be tethered to service in the militia. The majority rejected that claim. But even the majority recognized that there were lots of contexts in which the government could regulate gun ownership, including You know, keeping guns away from criminals, keeping guns away from the mentally imbalanced",
