    "turn_idx": 115,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm running for re-election. right now. I do have an opponent who's actually running against me, I think, on the gun safety issue. But Silver Spring and Tacoma Park are a progressive, democratic bastion in the state of Maryland. So I'm feeling good about my prospects for re-election. And I want to continue to fight hard for campaign finance reform, for the strongest possible environmental protections. We need to restore the Chesapeake Bay. We had basically no blue crab harvest this summer for the first time in my memory going back to my childhood. Any crabs that were eaten in Maryland this summer came from Louisiana, which is a shocker. So we might need to look at a moratorium on blue crab harvest and what else we can do to rescue that population. and I'm continuing to fight for the best possible education of the kids who live in Montgomery County and across the state. So, you know, I continue to be actively engaged in progressive politics and will hang around as long as my constituents will have me.",
